{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794445283,"nonce":"fZqOZTOqBjwJMpBSqt2LnTRbYc4=","message":"Item 7, the WebIDL form of the manifest, committed as 063d743, not pushed.\n\n`hxn_gen::webidl(\u0026library)` writes the API the JSON has, as WebIDL: an `interface` a class and a `namespace` a class of functions only; `constructor`, `static`; `undefined`, `boolean`, `byte` to `unsigned long long`, `float`, `double`, `USVString`, `Uint8Array`; `T?` for an `Option` of an interface; `Promise\u003cT\u003e` for a future; a `callback` for each lent function, named after where it is passed (`CounterEachF`), since WebIDL has no unnamed function type; `[Throws]` for a `Result`. Names are the Rust ones, as in the JSON, with an underscore before one WebIDL keeps for itself (`_byte`).\n\nWhat WebIDL has no word for is an extended attribute: HxnShared, HxnWeighed, HxnAsync, HxnBlocking, HxnMutating, HxnConsuming, HxnStream, HxnSignal, HxnAtomic, HxnSize, HxnKept, HxnExclusive.\n\nWhere they go was settled by the grammar. A return type takes no attribute, so a function returning `Stream\u003cT\u003e` is `[HxnStream]` on an operation returning `T`, not an annotated `sequence\u003cT\u003e`; the same for a signal, a cell and a size. The first version wrote `static [HxnStream] sequence\u003clong\u003e f()`, which is not WebIDL, and `sequence\u003cundefined\u003e` for a stream of nothing, which is not either.\n\nChecked by a parser: the user pointed out there is one in Rust. `weedle2` is a dev-dependency of hxn-gen, and the tests parse the fixture's WebIDL and every example's. It found one thing: `[Exposed=*]`, which the current WebIDL specification has and weedle2 5.0 does not parse. `Exposed` is about a browser's globals and says nothing of a native library, so it is not written. Installing a JavaScript parser to check with was tried first and blocked.\n\nWhere it is written: by the `hxn-gen` command as `\u003cname\u003e.hxn.webidl`, by `hxn build` under `\u003ctarget\u003e/hxn/\u003clibrary\u003e/`, and into a package. Only the fixture's is committed (`tests/counter/counter.hxn.webidl`), with a test that holds it to the source; the examples commit their JSON alone.\n\nNot done: reading WebIDL. The scope document's other use for it, a Rust trait skeleton generated from an externally specified API, is the reverse direction and nothing here does it. `hxn.Bind` reads the JSON.","files":null}]}